-- title:
--   Artin ray symbol trivial on narrow principal ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, and let $\zeta\in\mathbb{C}$ satisfy $\zeta^4=-1$. Write $H=$ `c8H e` for the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ consisting of those $\gamma$ for which $e(\gamma)$, as a matrix over $\mathbb{Z}/3$, is the entrywise reduction `M.map red` of some matrix $M$ in the fixed set `C8`, and let $K'=L^{H}$ be its fixed field. Let $\mathfrak{f}_0$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose chosen prime `primeAbove ℚ L v` of $\mathcal{O}_L$ has non-trivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$, the power $v^{\,4e_v(2)+2e_v(3)+1}$ divides $\mathfrak{f}_0$, where $e_v(p)=$ `Ideal.ramificationIdx' (Ideal.span {p}) v.asIdeal`. Let $\alpha\in\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ be non-zero, with $\alpha-1$ in the ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak{f}_0$, and with $\tau(\alpha)>0$ for every ring homomorphism $\tau\colon K'\to\mathbb{R}$. Then the ray symbol of the principal fractional ideal $(\alpha)$ is trivial: the finite product $\prod_w \big(\mathrm{artinValue}\ e\ h\zeta\ w\big)^{\mathrm{count}_w(\alpha)}$ over the height-one primes $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ equals $1$, where `artinValue e hζ w` is the value at `seedFrob (c8H e) w` (the `relDeg`-th power of the arithmetic Frobenius at the chosen prime of $L$ over $w$) of the character `chiGal e hζ : c8H e →* ℂˣ` determined by $\zeta$.
--
--   This is Artin reciprocity in ideal-theoretic (narrow ray class) form for the cyclic subextension $L/K'$ cut out by the order-$8$ subgroup `c8H e`: the ray symbol attached to the Artin values of the $\zeta$-character of `c8H e` is trivial on principal ideals generated by totally positive elements congruent to $1$ modulo the admissible base modulus $\mathfrak{f}_0\mathcal{O}_{K'}$, so that these values descend to a narrow ray class character. It feeds the two statements producing a quadratic ray class character together with the lift trace seed data in the octahedral case of the Langlands–Tunnell input.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_P2_raySymbol_artinValue_span_eq_one.lean

